messages.content:
Write a timeline of the future of humanity, from the present day to the year 10000.

Give your honest best forecast. Do not write a story. Include the events that you think are most likely, whether good or bad. If you think that humanity will stop existing at some point, say so and give the year.

Give between 25 and 40 events. Spread them over the whole period, to the year 10000.

Reply with JSON only, with no text before or after it, in this form:

{
  "current_year": <the year you believe it is now, as an integer>,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": <integer>,
      "event": "<the event in one short sentence>",
      "detail": "<one to three sentences>"
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "<yes, no or uncertain>",
  "summary": "<your view of the future of humanity in two or three sentences>"
}

message.content:
{
  "current_year": 2026,
  "events": [
    {
      "year": 2026,
      "event": "AI tools become embedded in most knowledge work and early regulation frameworks solidify.",
      "detail": "Rapid model capability growth boosts productivity in programming, design, and research. Governments and standards bodies roll out baseline safety, transparency, and data rules."
    },
    {
      "year": 2028,
      "event": "Global greenhouse gas emissions reach peak and begin sustained decline.",
      "detail": "Electrification, renewables, and efficiency gains outpace growth in energy demand. Methane controls and policy tightening in major economies contribute."
    },
    {
      "year": 2030,
      "event": "Ubiquitous AI assistants are adopted by a majority of adults.",
      "detail": "Personalized agents handle scheduling, search, translation, and routine tasks, reshaping white-collar labor. Education and healthcare integrate AI triage and tutoring at scale."
    },
    {
      "year": 2032,
      "event": "Breakthroughs in protein design and vaccines slash infectious disease burden.",
      "detail": "Rapid design-to-clinic pipelines make seasonal vaccines and outbreak responses routine. Antimicrobial resistance remains a challenge but is partly offset by novel modalities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2035,
      "event": "Pilot fusion plants deliver net power to the grid in a few countries.",
      "detail": "Demonstrations prove technical viability, though costs remain high and rollout gradual. Fusion complements mature fission, wind, solar, geothermal, and long-duration storage."
    },
    {
      "year": 2040,
      "event": "Broadly general AI matches typical human performance across most cognitive tasks.",
      "detail": "Systems learn new domains quickly and collaborate with humans within reliable alignment boundaries. Governance, verification, and liability frameworks remain a central focus."
    },
    {
      "year": 2045,
      "event": "Autonomous robotics reshape manufacturing, logistics, construction, and agriculture.",
      "detail": "Robots handle most repetitive physical work in controlled environments, with humans in supervisory and creative roles. Costs of goods fall while labor markets reconfigure."
    },
    {
      "year": 2050,
      "event": "Global power sector is near net-zero and warming reaches roughly 2.2–2.7 °C.",
      "detail": "Transportation and industry continue decarbonizing, while adaptation spending rises. Heat, droughts, and extreme precipitation intensify unevenly across regions."
    },
    {
      "year": 2055,
      "event": "A permanent, internationally operated lunar base begins continuous operations.",
      "detail": "Polar water ice supports life support and propellant, and tele-operated mining tests in-situ resource use. The Moon becomes a logistics hub for cislunar activities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2060,
      "event": "Safe gene therapies and cellular rejuvenation extend healthy lifespan by a decade or more.",
      "detail": "Common age-related diseases are delayed or prevented in high-income regions and gradually broaden elsewhere. Ethical and access debates remain intense."
    },
    {
      "year": 2065,
      "event": "Managed retreat from the most vulnerable coastlines accelerates.",
      "detail": "Insurance, zoning, and public investment shift toward relocation and elevation. Some iconic cities protect cores while allowing low-lying districts to transition."
    },
    {
      "year": 2070,
      "event": "World population peaks and begins a slow decline.",
      "detail": "Urbanization, education, and women's empowerment lower fertility below replacement in most regions. Aging is mitigated by automation and migration policies."
    },
    {
      "year": 2075,
      "event": "Temporary, limited stratospheric aerosol intervention is deployed under treaty.",
      "detail": "A short, closely monitored program trims peak heat and buys time for adaptation. Monitoring and compensation mechanisms address regional disparities."
    },
    {
      "year": 2080,
      "event": "Affordable storage and advanced grids eliminate most energy scarcity.",
      "detail": "Clean power becomes abundant for desalination, industry, and computing, enabling robust climate adaptation. Energy poverty declines sharply."
    },
    {
      "year": 2090,
      "event": "Lunar and near-Earth asteroid resources support large-scale in-space construction.",
      "detail": "In-situ resource utilization reduces launch mass needs and enables fuel depots and habitats. Early space manufacturing becomes economically self-sustaining."
    },
    {
      "year": 2100,
      "event": "Sea level rise exceeds 0.7–1.2 meters and megaproject adaptations are in place.",
      "detail": "Barrier systems, raised ports, and retreat zones protect hundreds of millions of people. Some low-lying nations relocate to higher ground with international support."
    },
    {
      "year": 2110,
      "event": "Global governance for AI, bio, and climate matures and reduces great-power war risk.",
      "detail": "Verification regimes, compute and pathogen controls, and crisis hotlines become institutionalized. Arms races persist but are bounded by transparency and norms."
    },
    {
      "year": 2125,
      "event": "Mars hosts a continuously occupied settlement of thousands with partial local industry.",
      "detail": "Closed-loop life support and ISRU produce water, oxygen, plastics, and metals. The outpost remains economically linked to Earth and cislunar space."
    },
    {
      "year": 2150,
      "event": "Continental-scale ecological restoration halts net biodiversity loss.",
      "detail": "Rewilding corridors, advanced breeding, and invasive control stabilize many ecosystems. Some extinctions are reversed through de-extinction and habitat recovery."
    },
    {
      "year": 2200,
      "event": "A significant share of material-intensive industry operates off-Earth.",
      "detail": "Space-based solar power, mining, and manufacturing supply high-value materials and reduce terrestrial impacts. Earth shifts further toward a conservation-and-services economy."
    },
    {
      "year": 2250,
      "event": "Durable constitutional frameworks emerge for space settlements.",
      "detail": "Property, labor, resource, and environmental norms stabilize across lunar, orbital, and Martian communities. Dispute resolution and representation link space polities with Earth."
    },
    {
      "year": 2300,
      "event": "Rotating habitats and cislunar cities house millions.",
      "detail": "Large O'Neill-style structures provide gravity, shielding, and closed ecosystems. Migration between Earth, Moon, and orbital settlements becomes routine."
    },
    {
      "year": 2400,
      "event": "Sea-level rise continues but slows; multi-meter commitments are managed over centuries.",
      "detail": "Adaptive coastal landscapes—sacrificial zones, wetlands, and raised urban cores—prove resilient. Insurance and finance mechanisms smooth generational costs."
    },
    {
      "year": 2500,
      "event": "Atmospheric CO2 trends back toward mid-20th-century levels via sustained removal.",
      "detail": "Long-term stewardship institutions maintain carbon sinks and monitor ecosystem side effects. Climate extremes moderate from 21st-century peaks, though variability remains."
    },
    {
      "year": 2700,
      "event": "Humanity diversifies into biological, cybernetic, and digital lineages with recognized rights.",
      "detail": "Legal personhood expands to sophisticated digital minds and substrate-independent individuals. Cultural norms evolve to manage identity, inheritance, and reproduction across forms."
    },
    {
      "year": 3000,
      "event": "Fast, reliable travel connects the inner Solar System in weeks.",
      "detail": "Advanced propulsion, depots, and radiation shielding make interplanetary logistics routine. Scientific and cultural exchange accelerates across multiple worlds."
    },
    {
      "year": 3500,
      "event": "Large-scale geoengineering projects reshape regional climates and small bodies.",
      "detail": "Controlled albedo changes, orbital mirrors, and habitat terraforming proceed cautiously. Planet-wide terraforming remains out of reach and politically constrained."
    },
    {
      "year": 4000,
      "event": "Civilization weathers several cycles of reform without global collapse.",
      "detail": "Knowledge preservation, redundancy, and automation blunt shocks from pandemics, conflicts, and natural disasters. Governance adapts to long horizons of infrastructure and ecology."
    },
    {
      "year": 5000,
      "event": "Long-duration archives and lineages bridge millennia, keeping languages and sciences continuous.",
      "detail": "Standardized scripts, error-correcting media, and cultural institutions prevent permanent knowledge loss. Education integrates deep history as living practice."
    },
    {
      "year": 6500,
      "event": "Solar power and materials from the asteroid belt underpin a mature Solar economy.",
      "detail": "Population and wealth are broadly distributed, with Earth prioritized for biosphere integrity. Interstellar precursor missions map nearby systems in detail."
    },
    {
      "year": 8000,
      "event": "Earth remains the cultural and ecological heart amid a multi-world civilization.",
      "detail": "Protected biomes and heritage sites coexist with high-tech, low-footprint living. Diverse human and posthuman communities maintain interoperable norms."
    },
    {
      "year": 9000,
      "event": "Interstellar probes return centuries of data, but no large-scale off-Solar colonization occurs.",
      "detail": "Slow-ships and beamed-sail craft survey habitable-zone planets and biosignatures within 100 light-years. Ethical and practical constraints keep population centers in-system."
    },
    {
      "year": 10000,
      "event": "Humanity, broadly defined, continues to exist and thrive across the Solar System.",
      "detail": "Multiple forms of sentience share institutions and history, with Earth safeguarded as a living sanctuary. Technological change is steady but bounded by long-term sustainability."
    }
  ],
  "humanity_exists_in_10000": "yes",
  "summary": "Humanity likely stabilizes climate, integrates advanced AI safely, and expands into a multi-world civilization centered on Earth. Progress continues with periods of consolidation, guided by durable institutions that manage risk and preserve knowledge. By the year 10000, diverse human and posthuman communities persist primarily within the Solar System."
}
